WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990
Five o'clock on a Friday.

2
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.580
The manager drops a report on the desk.

3
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.280
Everyone knows the
figures in it are wrong.

4
00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:09.300
Sign it off, she says.

5
00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:13.090
One by one, the workers
pick up the pen and sign.

6
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.570
Then it reaches the last worker.

7
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.330
The pen hovers over the page.

8
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.510
So what helps someone resist?

9
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.390
Brains?

10
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.340
Bravery?

11
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:23.720
Pure luck?

12
00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:28.480
In this mission, you'll see why pressure
is so hard to resist when everyone else

13
00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:32.010
agrees, or when an
authority gives the order.

14
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:36.020
You'll look back at classic
experiments on going along and obeying,

15
00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.750
and find out what made
people more likely to say no.

16
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.500
Your mission: find out what helps someone
stand firm when everyone else gives

17
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:44.930
in.
